  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math></p><p>Now we know that,</p><p>Non-negative integral solution of equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></math>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;are also possibilities</p><p>So by above formula we get,</p><p>Total number of non-negative solution will be,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>17</mn></mmultiscripts></math></p><p>Now solving&nbsp;If any of these <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> are equal<br />So, the equation will become<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math></p><p>Now finding possible cases we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>So, total possibilities where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi></math>&nbsp;are distinct will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>17</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>-</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>3</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>{Note adding&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;because the cases&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></math>&nbsp;is subtracted three times}</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>136</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>114</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
